<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stäfa</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Stafa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stäfa is a municipality on the north-eastern shore of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-zurich">Lake Zürich</a> in the canton of Zürich, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>. In the eighteenth century it was a prosperous village of vine-growers and textile workers, and in 1794–1795 it was the centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stafa-affair">Stäfa affair</a>, when its petition for rural rights was answered with military occupation and harsh sentences.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stafa.jpg" alt="Stäfa" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Roland zh · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:St%C3%A4fa_-_Z%C3%BCrichsee_-_ZSG_Limmat_2012-08-26_16-54-42.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
